{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Stop auto-deploy killing live code reviews: quiesce via a full-review drain window, and fail-NO-VOTE for retryable conditions\n\n## Problem\n\nThe continuous auto-deploy restarts the review-bot container while a code review is in\nflight, and the interrupted review casts a fail-closed `LLM-Review -1`. That vote then\nBLOCKS the automatic recovery which already exists, so every occurrence costs a human\nre-trigger. Observed FOUR times in one session (changes 1132/1189/1193/1208; three of four\nhad a `main` commit land mid-review; measured review durations 260-911s against a 45s\ndrain).\n\n### What the code actually does today (verified against source)\n\n* `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` ALREADY deploys only on change: `changed()` diffs\n  deployed-sha..target per path-class and rebuilds the bot only when `BOT_PATHS` /\n  `SECRETS_PATHS` changed (autodeploy.sh:219-230). \"Deploy only when the image changes\" is\n  already true — the unexplained 1193 collision needs a different explanation (candidates:\n  a SECRETS_PATHS-only refresh, or a backoff retry of a previously-failed target;\n  investigate during implementation and record on this ticket).\n* The shutdown drain ALREADY waits for the in-flight review: the lifespan does\n  `await queue.join()` bounded by `shutdown_drain_seconds()` (app.py:117) and the worker\n  marks the queue item done only after `review_and_vote` returns. The defect is purely the\n  CONSTANT: `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS = 45` (config.py:42) versus\n  `DEFAULT_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 1200` (config.py:30). A deploy landing mid-review\n  times out the drain at 45s, cancels the worker, and the teardown-corrupted review\n  fail-closes a `-1`.\n* The backfill reconciler (`reconcile.py`) re-drives any CURRENT revision with NO\n  `LLM-Review` vote, on startup and every 300s. Casting the fail-closed `-1` makes the\n  change invisible to it — the veto disables the recovery designed for this failure.\n\n## Change 1 — quiesce: size the drain to a full review (operator-approved 20 min)\n\nRaise `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` from 45 to 1200 (= the per-review timeout — the\nprincipled bound: the drain exists to let the in-flight review finish, and the review is\nalready wall-clock-bounded by `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`). Resize\n`stop_grace_period` in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` per its existing derivation\n(drain + store write-lock budget + push reconcile lock): 1200 + 60 + 45 -> 1320s, updating\nthe derivation comment.\n`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_reviewbot_stop_grace_period_covers_an_in_flight_store_write`\nreads both values from source and enforces the relationship — it must pass unmodified.\n\nCost when no review is in flight: none (`queue.join()` returns immediately on an empty\nqueue). Cost when one is in flight: the deploy waits for it — that is the point (the\nKubernetes terminationGracePeriodSeconds/preStop pattern). The 2-minute timer cadence\nstays: a deploy that quiesces is safe at any cadence, and autodeploy already no-ops on an\nunchanged target.\n\n## Change 2 — fail-NO-VOTE for retryable coverage gaps, with a bounded escalation\n\nMatches how Zuul (jobs interrupted by an executor restart are retried without reporting)\nand Prow (evicted jobs are rescheduled) behave; the bounded retry mirrors Zuul's\nRETRY_LIMIT.\n\n* `adapter.code_review_decision` already classifies every non-PASS outcome\n  (`_TAG_SUFFIXES` / `_coverage_gap_reason`). Thread the machine-readable sub-reason out\n  of `_block` as a new `gap_reason` key on the decision dict (None for PASS/finding).\n* In `voter.review_and_vote`, when the decision is a coverage-gap BLOCK with a RETRYABLE\n  `gap_reason` — `review-error`, `llm-unavailable`, `scanner`, `gate-disabled` — do NOT\n  post the vote. Record the attempt in a new `review_attempts` table beside the dedup\n  ledger (`dedup.py` SQLite, keyed `(change_id, revision)`), emit a distinct greppable\n  `REVIEW_RETRY_DEFERRED` marker, and return. The change stays vote-less, so the EXISTING\n  backfill reconciler re-drives it within `RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS` — no reconciler\n  change needed.\n* `indeterminate` is TERMINAL (vote the `-1`): by CI-system semantics a review that RAN TO\n  COMPLETION and concluded \"cannot establish coverage\" is a result, not an interruption.\n  `finding` is unchanged. The merge-path `_merge_coverage_gap_decision` keeps its current\n  fail-closed vote in this ticket: it deliberately gets NO `gap_reason` key (its REST\n  failures are pre-review setup; revisit separately if it recurs), and the voter's\n  deferral protocol keys strictly on `gap_reason` being present and retryable.\n* Bounded escalation: when `review_attempts` reaches the cap (new\n  `RETRYABLE_GAP_MAX_ATTEMPTS`, default 3, env-overridable via `ReceiverConfig`), cast the\n  fail-closed `-1` with the original reason's tag plus an appended \"automatic retries\n  exhausted\" note (tag VOCABULARY unchanged — the tag test keeps passing), and emit the\n  existing `VOTER_ERROR` marker so the `rebar/host:voter_errors` alarm surface fires.\n  The attempts store is deliberately shaped for ticket bb9b's contributor re-trigger to\n  RESET (shared retry budget). Reset semantics: `reset_attempts(change_id, revision)`\n  DELETES the row (no status flags, no zeroed counters left behind) — after a reset the\n  store is indistinguishable from \"never attempted\". The attempt is recorded (INSERT/\n  increment) BEFORE the deferral `return`; a SQLite failure on that write is caught and\n  logged as `VOTER_ERROR` and the deferral still returns vote-less (an uncounted attempt\n  only delays escalation by one cycle — fail-open on the counter, never on the vote).\n* Teardown mid-review needs no separate discriminator: the deferral decision happens\n  before any vote POST, so a teardown-corrupted review that fail-closes as `review-error`\n  is deferred vote-less, and with Change 1 the cancel almost never lands mid-review at\n  all.\n\n### Constraints (both verified as part of implementation)\n\n1. **No silent-pass hole.** Vote-less stays unsubmittable (submit REQUIRES `LLM-Review +1`);\n   assert no reconciler degraded mode turns \"no vote\" into \"submittable\".\n2. **Genuinely vote-less.** The deferral posts NOTHING to the change (no provisional\n   comment), or the reconciler's no-vote pre-filter would be re-suppressed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py` — drain default 45 -> 1200; new\n  `RETRYABLE_GAP_MAX_ATTEMPTS`.\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` — `stop_grace_period` 150s -> 1320s + derivation\n  comment.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py` — `gap_reason` on the decision dict.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` — defer-not-vote for retryable gaps + bounded\n  escalation.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/dedup.py` — the `review_attempts` table: `record_attempt` /\n  `attempt_count` keyed `(change_id, revision)`, and `reset_attempts` = DELETE the row.\n  This table is SEPARATE from the existing `voted` table; the deferred path writes ONLY\n  to `review_attempts`, never to `voted`.\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — regenerate for the new env var (the committed registry is drift-\n  gated by `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py::test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree`).\n- `docs/review-policy.md` — document the retryable/terminal split and the escalation.\n- Tests in `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` (see below).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` is 1200 and compose `stop_grace_period` is\n      1320s; `test_reviewbot_stop_grace_period_covers_an_in_flight_store_write` passes\n      unmodified.\n- [ ] AC2: a coverage-gap decision with `gap_reason` in {review-error, llm-unavailable,\n      scanner, gate-disabled} casts NO vote, records an attempt, and posts nothing to the\n      change, and emits the greppable `REVIEW_RETRY_DEFERRED` marker — asserted by a\n      unit test per reason.\n- [ ] AC3: `indeterminate` and `finding` still cast the `-1`, and PASS still casts the\n      `+1` — asserted by tests (no behaviour change for terminal outcomes).\n- [ ] AC4: the Nth (default 3rd) consecutive retryable failure on the same\n      `(change_id, revision)` casts the fail-closed `-1` with the \"retries exhausted\" note\n      and emits `VOTER_ERROR` — asserted by a test; the cap is env-overridable.\n- [ ] AC5: the deferred path leaves the change eligible for the backfill reconciler — no\n      row in the `voted` table and no Gerrit vote (the `review_attempts` row from AC2 is\n      expected and does NOT suppress re-drive) — asserted by a test driving the\n      reconciler over a deferred change.\n- [ ] AC6: `docs/review-policy.md` documents the retryable/terminal split, the bound, and\n      the escalation surface.\n- [ ] AC7: `docs/env-vars.md` is regenerated and committed (its drift-gate test passes),\n      and `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the review-bot test module pass.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\nFrom the worktree venv:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## Relationship to bb9b\n\n`bb9b-608f-0183-4ca5` (lands second) gives contributors a manual re-trigger for any\nremaining `-1` that is not a real finding — including this ticket's escalated `-1` —\nimplemented as \"reset the shared `review_attempts` budget + force re-review\". This ticket\ndeliberately shapes the attempts store for that reuse."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785699199640045001,"uuid":"135c1007-d918-4e47-a03a-6cc9e830f105"}